<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Document xmlns:p="property" xmlns:r="reflection" Id="JVFMzrtTIhFhp68f77n65y" LanguageVersion="2025.7.4" Version="0.128">
  <NugetDependency Id="SIMDywDLwNbQ5UdOPHQxYD" Location="VL.CoreLib" Version="2025.7.4" />
  <NugetDependency Id="Sm17wEPgUJCVB75op3gzPF" Location="VL.Skia" Version="2025.7.4" />
  <NugetDependency Id="CCoTJSCcdlnfZwmjUnPFVB" Location="VL.Mapsui" Version="0.0.0" />
  <!--
    NetTopologySuite is declared HERE, by this document, and that is not the same as VL.Mapsui
    declaring it. VL.Mapsui's own declaration is what lets its node signatures name NTS types; a
    patch that wants to use NTS nodes itself needs its own dependency on it. Measured: without this
    line the node below is "Not found"; with it, it resolves.
  -->
  <NugetDependency Id="KkbVvAgR3UtmSGnGV4pAoR" Location="NetTopologySuite" Version="2.6.0" />
  <!--
    VL.NetTopologySuite is the package that MAKES geometry; this one draws it. VL.Mapsui's nuspec
    depends on it so that opening this patch does not greet you with red nodes - vvvv does not
    fetch a missing document dependency by itself, it shows it red and offers to install on
    rightclick.
  -->
  <NugetDependency Id="QVnZMbPyNO4lv6YFocyiqT" Location="VL.NetTopologySuite" Version="0.0.1-alpha" />
  <Patch Id="FJzZkKqVfW12i9kQk6L0hz">
    <Canvas Id="N0E8bKG5vqG1aLaGsfcogC" DefaultCategory="Main" CanvasType="FullCategory" />
    <!--

    ************************ Application ************************

-->
    <Node Name="Application" Bounds="100,100" Id="Pt4eKK7Ag0dikcitT4Vmar">
      <p:NodeReference>
        <Choice Kind="ContainerDefinition" Name="Process" />
        <FullNameCategoryReference ID="Primitive" />
      </p:NodeReference>
      <Patch Id="T1yChjTcVpcQLJ4rxMEL44">
        <Canvas Id="VxYLn5bECvkjhyGerEE3sc" CanvasType="Group">
          <Pad Id="VaZNqihOnpwz6dORWEdpu0" Bounds="60,30,620,200" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Drawing many features - define the type once, and every place is an instance.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;THE PATCH DOES NOT GROW WITH THE DATA, AND THIS ONE PROVES IT. Turn Count up to 2000 and restart: two thousand places appear and not one node, not one link changes. That is the claim, and a patch that wired three places by hand could only assert it.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;A RECORD IS THE TYPE, AN INSTANCE IS A PLACE. Landmark is defined on the right - right-click the canvas and pick Record to make one of your own. It has a Geometry and two words about it. Add a property to the record and every instance has it, including the two thousand.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;THE FOREACH IS WHERE THEY ARE MADE. Two RandomSpreads scatter Count longitudes and Count latitudes; the region takes one of each per iteration and builds one Landmark, and the splicer at the bottom collects them into a Spread. Name and Type cross the border WITHOUT a splicer, so every instance shares them - that is what a link straight through the edge means.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;TOFEATURES IS THE ONLY THING BETWEEN YOUR TYPE AND THE MAP. It reads each value's properties: the one whose type is Geometry is the shape, and every other property becomes an attribute under the name the record gives it. So LabelStyle looks up &quot;Name&quot; and the record is the only place that word is written. Watch Status - it says how many it made and, if a type has no geometry or two and no way to choose, it says that instead of drawing nothing.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;WHAT RUNS ONCE, AND HOW YOU CAN TELL. The generator, the record constructors and the spread all sit in the CREATE operation. They run when the patch starts and never again; the spread lands in a Pad - storage that survives to the next frame - and Update only reads it. CONVERSIONS COUNTS THE PROOF: it reaches 1 and stays at 1 no matter how long you drag and zoom. Move the same nodes into Update and it climbs once per frame.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;How that is expressed in the document: the Create operation names ONE thing, the link that writes the spread into the Pad. Everything that link depends on comes along with it. Everything not named runs every frame - which is what an empty Create means, and what most patches have.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;WHY IT MATTERS AT THIS SIZE. Measured on 1000 features of 500 vertices each: when the same spread arrives every frame, everything downstream costs 0.013 ms per frame. When the features are rebuilt every frame instead, just MAKING them costs 43 ms - two and a half frames, before anything is drawn. Four thousand times, decided by nothing but where the construction sits.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;The price of building once is that it does not react: changing Count or a Name does nothing until you restart with F8 then F5. That is the correct trade for data read from a file. If you want it to rebuild when its inputs change - and only then - that is what a Cache region is for.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;WHAT A POINT LOOKS LIKE IS SymbolStyle's JOB. Shape, Scale and two colours - and it REPLACES VectorStyle rather than joining it, because Mapsui's SymbolStyle derives from VectorStyle. Without one a point is still drawn, but only as a ring: measured, the fallback covers 180 pixels where a filled marker covers 952. Scale 1 is 32 pixels, and a symbol is drawn in PIXELS - zoom in and the markers stay the same size while the ground under them does not.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;THAT IS RIGHT FOR A MARKER AND WRONG FOR A MEASUREMENT, and Mapsui gives you no switch: its UnitType property exists but its Skia renderer never reads it - measured, four renders, all 1156 pixels. So when the size IS the information - a 500 metre catchment, a GPS accuracy, an area affected - do not look for a pin. BUFFER THE POINT INTO A POLYGON with VL.NetTopologySuite and style it with VectorStyle. It then scales with the map because it IS on the map, and unlike a symbol you can pick it, measure it and intersect it.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;THE LABEL STEPS ASIDE FOR THE MARKER, AND NOBODY HAD TO SAY SO. Mapsui centres a label on the feature it names, which is right for a polygon and wrong for a point wearing a symbol - the text and the marker end up in the same pixels. LabelStyle can see the SymbolStyle wired into it, so it reads the scale, works out the radius and lifts the label clear by that much plus 4 pixels. Change Scale and the label moves with it. Wire LabelStyle to a polygon fill instead and nothing moves, because a polygon's label belongs at its centre.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;LABELS AT TWO HUNDRED POINTS ARE STILL NOISE, and that part no setting fixes. They no longer cover their own markers, but they cover EACH OTHER, and Mapsui's CollisionDetection does nothing on this render path - measured, eight overlapping labels draw the same 763 pixels with it on and with it off. This is cartography rather than a defect: no map labels two hundred things at once. The real answer is to draw labels only past a zoom level, which is what MinVisible and MaxVisible are for and is not a node here yet. For now, empty LabelStyle's Attribute pin to turn them off; a style with nothing named has nothing to write.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;The Geometry slot in the record is marked yellow: &quot;This field could mutate at runtime&quot;. It is a warning and nothing more - a Record is immutable and NetTopologySuite's Geometry is an ordinary class, so VL is right to say so, and vvvv's own shipped records do the same (VL.Skia's paint holds an SKShader). Just never modify a Geometry after it is inside a Landmark.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Geometry comes from VL.NetTopologySuite, as everywhere here: this package draws geometry and does not create it. Coordinate and Point are two of its nodes; a GeoJSON or Shapefile reader would be where a real two thousand came from.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Enabled starts OFF on the tile layer. Opening a document in vvvv runs it, so a map that fetched on open would give you no chance to decline.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Watch Layers Built: it should settle at 1 and stay. A number climbing frame after frame means something rebuilds the layer every frame, and every rebuild starts a fresh round of tile requests. Close vvvv if you see it climb.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Where to go next: HowTo Label your data for attributes built by hand, which is the right shape when the columns are only known at runtime. HowTo Pick what you clicked to ask the map which of these you are pointing at.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="UnaIkq8cPr0a4UZQVn7ji7" Comment="Enabled" Bounds="79,280,35,35" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="false">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="ImmutableTypeFlag" Name="Boolean" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:buttonmode p:Assembly="VL.UI.Forms" p:Type="VL.HDE.PatchEditor.Editors.ButtonModeEnum">Toggle</p:buttonmode>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="CNYLiTg3BUtmCJlFwHyUjv" Comment="Cache To Disk" Bounds="207,280,35,35" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="true">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="ImmutableTypeFlag" Name="Boolean" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:buttonmode p:Assembly="VL.UI.Forms" p:Type="VL.HDE.PatchEditor.Editors.ButtonModeEnum">Toggle</p:buttonmode>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Node Bounds="79,340,150,19" Id="JqwwJBWIvaSJq4DTAz8vuN">
            <p:NodeReference LastCategoryFullName="Mapsui.Layers" LastDependency="VL.Mapsui.vl">
              <Choice Kind="NodeFlag" Name="Node" Fixed="true" />
              <Choice Kind="ProcessAppFlag" Name="OpenStreetMap" />
            </p:NodeReference>
            <Pin Id="Usi9xynIVqJWvRhEvGVOYQ" Name="Enabled" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="ARy89W2GJw4s60rzwfmBsV" Name="Cache" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="VE109xy4WqBycyAwxMeCrD" Name="Result" Kind="OutputPin" />
            <Pin Id="MVGJGduk0mPWJznoGv9YVX" Name="Layers Built" Kind="OutputPin" />
            <Pin Id="HwRnfleRlGfpKEI7pXlafv" Name="Cache Status" Kind="OutputPin" />
          </Node>
          <Pad Id="RgIIgaq8NiTBppqeaxZgPe" Comment="Layers Built" Bounds="153,391,80,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" />
          <Node Bounds="87,523,39,19" Id="IuHPlniMpFcdUZg9WNt7Xp">
            <p:NodeReference LastCategoryFullName="Collections.Spread" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="NodeFlag" Name="Node" Fixed="true" />
              <Choice Kind="OperationCallFlag" Name="Cons" />
              <CategoryReference Kind="RecordType" Name="Spread" NeedsToBeDirectParent="true" />
            </p:NodeReference>
            <Pin Id="FitnqKKJuItGI6PwD5m2Mp" Name="Input" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="Udad8igNKGlXkj4SIfvVV8" Name="Input 2" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="Obo0KlAOX8uJTLEhkSgG4Y" Name="Result" Kind="OutputPin" />
          </Node>
          <Pad Id="QTNlTyezfmbasb8gEcPG61" Comment="Initial Longitude" Bounds="140,583,62,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="135.7581">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="Float64" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="I8MAlGEJKxag8SUuQTLx71" Comment="Initial Latitude" Bounds="229,544,62,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="34.9859">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="Float64" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="MU5GcscWwFrk45xrCPm07u" Comment="Initial Zoom Level" Bounds="329,583,50,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="15">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="Integer32" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
          </Pad>
          <!--
            ***** your own shapes, from here down *****

            The shape has to come from somewhere, and that somewhere is NOT VL.Mapsui: this package
            draws geometry, it does not create it. In a real patch the geometry comes from VL.GIS,
            from a file, or from a service. Here it is a fixture so the example stands on its own.

            Read WKT is one way in and the shortest one to read on a page. VL.NetTopologySuite also
            builds geometry coordinate by coordinate - Coordinate, LinearRing, Polygon - and its own
            HowTo Create a polygon shows that. Either way what arrives here is the same type, which
            is the point: geometry is a TYPE, not a format.
          -->





          <!--
            ***** what makes a label possible *****

            A Feature is geometry PLUS attributes, and this is the attributes half finally being
            used. Dictionary Add builds one entry: leave its Input unconnected and you start from an
            empty dictionary, which is what the type's default is.

            The key is what LabelStyle will look up. Change "name" to something else in both places
            and the map labels itself with that instead.
          -->




          <!--
            A SECOND attribute: the first Add's Output goes into the second Add's Input, and one
            feature now carries two. Only the FIRST Add in a chain leaves its Input unconnected -
            that is where the empty dictionary comes from.
          -->






          <!--
            ***** a second feature on the SAME layer *****

            One layer, two features, one style - and two different labels, because LabelColumn names
            an attribute rather than carrying the text. That is the whole point of it.
          -->










          <!--

    ************************ Landmark ************************

            A RECORD: the same two attributes, said once instead of typed twice.

            Right-click the canvas and pick Record to make one of these. Give it properties, and
            their names ARE the attribute names - ToAttributes reads them off the type, so nothing
            has to be spelled twice and nothing can be spelled differently.

            Compare it with the two Dictionary Add chains above. Those are the right shape when the
            columns are only known at runtime - a GeoJSON file, a service, a Shapefile. This is the
            right shape when the data already has one.
-->
          <Node Name="Landmark" Bounds="1340,430" Id="FeJlDEUULfslHALSuuik7c">
            <p:NodeReference LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="Builtin">
              <Choice Kind="RecordDefinition" Name="Record" />
            </p:NodeReference>
            <Patch Id="TzPaxkDm79YTHGYrVvNDF1">
              <Canvas Id="O0rvVBY3J5g54gWSEG3x1C" CanvasType="Group">
                <Pad Id="HszeGVhlk5Lnu9yvCsBUdK" SlotId="Rb1iAAA719wzKFpoEnacUw" Bounds="949,738" />
                <Pad Id="EqHYCvXAychZiD2bmOvD2W" SlotId="B8TrRsdCNGWxPaGbJ2Sm8M" Bounds="1065,739" />
                <Pad Id="GCY5MpeTOxYFLDDWGcNXoU" SlotId="MNKi6jBQtpEpBeS6vlaC9s" Bounds="1181,739" />
                <ControlPoint Id="KhlpdPEKP0HEDszyuhiRjI" Bounds="949,708" />
                <ControlPoint Id="GqiX0KtU6KATE2l0qUZw3X" Bounds="949,768" />
                <ControlPoint Id="CtFCDrxrYEse7jDSlwmX5H" Bounds="1065,709" />
                <ControlPoint Id="TvAx8OHx8pCGDCd2Pp2Ndl" Bounds="1065,769" />
                <ControlPoint Id="Tyor7YBRlosbsQOIR8IdBS" Bounds="1181,709" />
                <ControlPoint Id="LXyxdN2h2emR6PEujSEy84" Bounds="1181,769" />
              </Canvas>
              <Patch Id="DRhrVEWa1bfkJfyEhU7Ss0" Name="Create">
                <Pin Id="GNiTW5CyddsxtvLTy47vNG" Name="Name" Kind="InputPin" />
                <Pin Id="G6hzrhGYS4JVMZofYbIp23" Name="Type" Kind="InputPin" />
                <Pin Id="KTuTZdm2cMfM7PnnmpqvPe" Name="Geometry" Kind="InputPin" />
              </Patch>
              <ProcessDefinition Id="Fm2Qy6jSBt8Pizj1X8yF1q" IsHidden="true">
                <Fragment Id="DRCQY08KG2fE4NGbHFMb14" Patch="DRhrVEWa1bfkJfyEhU7Ss0" Enabled="true" />
                <Fragment Id="RCenCNm9HPdS06c3Zts9io" Patch="S7UsB6wWmD2poxvHlhONMD" />
              </ProcessDefinition>
              <Slot Id="Rb1iAAA719wzKFpoEnacUw" Name="Name">
                <p:TypeAnnotation p:Type="TypeReference">
                  <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
                </p:TypeAnnotation>
              </Slot>
              <Slot Id="B8TrRsdCNGWxPaGbJ2Sm8M" Name="Type">
                <p:TypeAnnotation p:Type="TypeReference">
                  <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
                </p:TypeAnnotation>
              </Slot>
              <!--
                This slot is marked YELLOW in the editor: "This field could mutate at runtime."
                A Record is immutable, and NetTopologySuite's Geometry is an ordinary .NET class
                with SRID, Apply and Normalize on it, so VL is right. It is a WARNING and nothing
                more - the check is read by the editor's diagnostics and by no other part of the
                compiler, and vvvv's own shipped records do the same thing constantly (VL.Skia's
                SkiaPaint holds an SKShader, HDE's widgets hold SKImage, VL.Stride holds a Texture).

                The one real hazard is serialization, and NonSerialized below is exactly how
                VL.Skia guards its SKShader slot. Do not mutate a Geometry after putting it in a
                Landmark: records are shared by reference, so two Landmarks made from one would
                both change and nothing downstream would notice.
              -->
              <Slot Id="MNKi6jBQtpEpBeS6vlaC9s" Name="Geometry">
                <p:Attributes>
                  <AttributeData>
                    <p:TypeReference LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
                      <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="NonSerializedAttribute" />
                    </p:TypeReference>
                  </AttributeData>
                </p:Attributes>
                <p:TypeAnnotation p:Type="TypeReference">
                  <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="Geometry" />
                </p:TypeAnnotation>
              </Slot>
              <Link Id="N5yRnA1Ntnnny7R8LadEcY" Ids="GNiTW5CyddsxtvLTy47vNG,KhlpdPEKP0HEDszyuhiRjI" IsHidden="true" />
              <Link Id="HeSI6hSu9UPqcqQYwEsSrm" Ids="KhlpdPEKP0HEDszyuhiRjI,HszeGVhlk5Lnu9yvCsBUdK" />
              <Patch Id="S7UsB6wWmD2poxvHlhONMD" Name="Split">
                <Pin Id="FFdYICEEPchy4zxczWK3f5" Name="Name" Kind="OutputPin" />
                <Pin Id="MRmpPCtSq0Hr26JwHXUEJy" Name="Type" Kind="OutputPin" />
                <Pin Id="C29zuRg8UwYfjzDePhQK60" Name="Geometry" Kind="OutputPin" />
              </Patch>
              <Link Id="EZtjyncf5FeVr79h1fLKkV" Ids="GqiX0KtU6KATE2l0qUZw3X,FFdYICEEPchy4zxczWK3f5" IsHidden="true" />
              <Link Id="OOo4xQD36e0HF9vUNHQtil" Ids="HszeGVhlk5Lnu9yvCsBUdK,GqiX0KtU6KATE2l0qUZw3X" />
              <Link Id="EHMgdJqA2tG1YT4yYiCQgU" Ids="G6hzrhGYS4JVMZofYbIp23,CtFCDrxrYEse7jDSlwmX5H" IsHidden="true" />
              <Link Id="TtdrXiJOSuuNZboLSMTYpn" Ids="CtFCDrxrYEse7jDSlwmX5H,EqHYCvXAychZiD2bmOvD2W" />
              <Link Id="QRt1E25EQREL989Uwuun9z" Ids="TvAx8OHx8pCGDCd2Pp2Ndl,MRmpPCtSq0Hr26JwHXUEJy" IsHidden="true" />
              <Link Id="CVA5gHMCX7IpjBgngJIgQo" Ids="EqHYCvXAychZiD2bmOvD2W,TvAx8OHx8pCGDCd2Pp2Ndl" />
              <Link Id="JEBonRGgoIUFYxE5cEOKro" Ids="KTuTZdm2cMfM7PnnmpqvPe,Tyor7YBRlosbsQOIR8IdBS" IsHidden="true" />
              <Link Id="MiWxzmVpCe89EjfAk7gFLl" Ids="Tyor7YBRlosbsQOIR8IdBS,GCY5MpeTOxYFLDDWGcNXoU" />
              <Link Id="GYyZIN4sUcDmOvyXPFtt6k" Ids="LXyxdN2h2emR6PEujSEy84,C29zuRg8UwYfjzDePhQK60" IsHidden="true" />
              <Link Id="Nzu3RJUPnc0aDANyzL7Goa" Ids="GCY5MpeTOxYFLDDWGcNXoU,LXyxdN2h2emR6PEujSEy84" />
            </Patch>
          </Node>




          <Pad Id="Oul3T6VWihMkGR8vkoY0vO" Comment="Name" Bounds="1580,510,120,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Nijo Castle">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="FZ12eSIDP9mGP0FmE5IcsR" Comment="Type" Bounds="1580,535,120,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="castle">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
          </Pad>


          <!-- the second and third places: the same type again, nothing new wired -->








          <!--
            ***** the one node between your data and the map *****

            ToFeatures reads each value's properties: the one typed Geometry is the shape, every
            other one becomes an attribute under the name the record gives it. So LabelStyle looks up
            "Name" and the record is the only place that word appears.

            Its Status output says what it found - and says so out loud if a type has no geometry, or
            has two and cannot tell which to draw.

            THIS IS WHERE A THOUSAND WOULD GO. The pin takes a spread, so the patch does not grow
            with the data: three instances here, or ten thousand rows read from a file, arrive the
            same way and the node count is identical.
          -->
          <Node Bounds="1180,660,110,19" Id="Gwsi9PjdKOE9Li7A6rkWd5">
            <p:NodeReference LastCategoryFullName="Mapsui" LastDependency="VL.Mapsui.vl">
              <Choice Kind="NodeFlag" Name="Node" Fixed="true" />
              <Choice Kind="ProcessAppFlag" Name="ToFeatures" />
            </p:NodeReference>
            <Pin Id="SAorVJSP3Q1oFhAqIQdvLD" Name="Values" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="G69LMqZBByDHYApccyPL9W" Name="Result" Kind="OutputPin" />
            <Pin Id="JrM5Yua7jXqgKQWbu3hp06" Name="Status" Kind="OutputPin" />
            <Pin Id="R8Tfi6mnlNJT9S92pM4vwh" Name="Conversions" Kind="OutputPin" />
          </Node>
          <!--
            THE NUMBER THAT PROVES IT. Conversions counts how often the data was actually converted.
            With the construction in the Create fragment it reaches 1 and stays there forever. Move
            the same nodes back into Update and it climbs once per frame - which is invisible with
            three landmarks and fatal with three thousand.
          -->
          <Pad Id="He1dSPYXLNpYKCZhEgRUzP" Comment="Conversions - should stay at 1" Bounds="1310,690,200,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" />
          <!--
            ***** where the many come from *****

            Two RandomSpreads scatter Count longitudes and Count latitudes around Kyoto. Turn Count
            up to 2000 and nothing below changes - not one node, not one link. That is the claim
            this patch exists to make, and it is the only honest way to make it.

            Count is read in the CREATE operation, so it takes effect when the patch starts. Change
            it and restart (F8 then F5) to see a different number of places. A patch that wanted to
            react while running would put this in a Cache region instead.
          -->
          <Pad Id="FS4AuQsy1yhpQm29QMxTOW" Comment="Count" Bounds="1180,300,62,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="200">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="Integer32" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
          </Pad>
          <Node Bounds="1180,340,85,19" Id="QJONevYEsEhWvYNwgjgCte">
            <p:NodeReference LastCategoryFullName="Collections.Spread" LastDependency="VL.Collections.vl">
              <Choice Kind="NodeFlag" Name="Node" Fixed="true" />
              <Choice Kind="ProcessAppFlag" Name="RandomSpread" />
            </p:NodeReference>
            <Pin Id="NpJYqcpgq1CmI7VfR278ab" Name="Center" Kind="InputPin" DefaultValue="135.7581" />
            <Pin Id="IUm0cVo55Xegij17cvboFB" Name="Width" Kind="InputPin" DefaultValue="0.06" />
            <Pin Id="CE3EjND4ORVmCYQHSb22FU" Name="Seed" Kind="InputPin" DefaultValue="1" />
            <Pin Id="C5fDhFs0AeGhEzStRM7z44" Name="Count" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="O33XlNRRiKrpKlhAeg0FQq" Name="Output" Kind="OutputPin" />
          </Node>
          <Node Bounds="1320,340,85,19" Id="CuJvFLiMLgcRmSC33iY3fg">
            <p:NodeReference LastCategoryFullName="Collections.Spread" LastDependency="VL.Collections.vl">
              <Choice Kind="NodeFlag" Name="Node" Fixed="true" />
              <Choice Kind="ProcessAppFlag" Name="RandomSpread" />
            </p:NodeReference>
            <Pin Id="SXWf1zHLLS3WdT7ZeJ1CQR" Name="Center" Kind="InputPin" DefaultValue="34.9859" />
            <Pin Id="K29L5uVl0nBOPSBJuQBbQo" Name="Width" Kind="InputPin" DefaultValue="0.045" />
            <Pin Id="OZoEFV8IOht41Zuwzm8mEo" Name="Seed" Kind="InputPin" DefaultValue="2" />
            <Pin Id="CJ00WE6fttBHGvd1Zsrkls" Name="Count" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="AvOGKbZt7UoNXcEl2PZI00" Name="Output" Kind="OutputPin" />
          </Node>

          <!--
            ***** one Landmark per item *****

            A ForEach region: the two spreads enter through the splicers at the top and arrive
            inside as ONE longitude and ONE latitude, and each Landmark leaving through the splicer
            at the bottom is collected into a Spread of them.

            Name and Type are linked straight through the border with no splicer, so every instance
            shares them. Give the record more properties and they all ride along the same way.
          -->
          <Node Bounds="1180,400,300,240" Id="Jzl9NudfyluYfv0G0qX93v">
            <p:NodeReference LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="Builtin">
              <Choice Kind="StatefulRegion" Name="Region (Stateful)" Fixed="true" />
              <Choice Kind="ApplicationStatefulRegion" Name="ForEach" />
              <CategoryReference Kind="Category" Name="Primitive" />
            </p:NodeReference>
            <Pin Id="HnUO06eRXmM2VNI7AFYtY5" Name="Break" Kind="OutputPin" />
            <ControlPoint Id="TagwBtA8domnoQuutAfeFt" Bounds="1200,407" Alignment="Top" />
            <ControlPoint Id="BQLocIaeu6O5JOHxRU8yCF" Bounds="1260,407" Alignment="Top" />
            <ControlPoint Id="D5yQwnSl1RsXaPGRjJvip5" Bounds="1220,635" Alignment="Bottom" />
            <Patch Id="CNcjz6LmHUgKTjlMev57kt" ManuallySortedPins="true">
